{number: 42}
{title: I Gave My Life for Thee}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] I gave My life for thee, My precious blood I [G7] shed,
That [C] thou might'st ransomed [F] be, And [C] quickened [G7] from the [C] dead;
[G] I gave, I [C] gave My [G] life for [C] thee,
What [F] hast thou [C] given [G7] for [C] Me?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
My [C] Father's house of light, My glory-circled [G7] throne,
I [C] left for earthly [F] night, For [C] wand'rings [G7] sad and [C] lone;
[G] I left, I [C] left it [G] all for [C] thee,
Hast [F] thou left [C] aught for [G7] Me? [C]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
I [C] suffered much for thee, More than thy tongue can [G7] tell,
Of [C] bitt'rest ago-[F] ny, To [C] rescue [G7] thee from [C] hell;
[G] I've borne, I've [C] borne it [G] all for [C] thee,
What [F] hast thou [C] borne for [G7] Me? [C]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
And [C] I have brought to thee, Down from My home a-[G7] bove,
Sal-[C] vation full and [F] free, My [C] pardon [G7] and My [C] love;
[G] I bring, I [C] bring rich [G] gifts to [C] thee,
What [F] hast thou [C] brought to [G7] Me? [C]
{end_of_verse}
